    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "01\nReturned error\nAfter a reattachment is accepted, a failing completion now exposes that attempt’s error. Before, the first connection error survived both reattachment failure paths.\nUnexplained\nThis consequence of the loop rewrite is absent from the PR’s stated decisions.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "02\nFixture translations\nTest adapters reinterpret old knobs: client inline=0 becomes 64 KiB, the client directory is precreated, and workspace memoryCapBytes is accepted but unused. Other spill fixtures change thresholds and record splits.\nUnexplained\nAdapters are stated; these particular translations and their changed exercise of storage paths are unexplained.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "03\nTest oracles\nThe old resource-policy test block is deleted. Package policy checks already existed. Logger / spool / lifetime expectations now read the policy; added tests exercise selected consumer overrides, retry counts, and timeout purposes.\nUnexplained\nNo specific reason is recorded for deleting that block or changing these expectation sources.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "04\nRequired inputs\nDaemonPolicy already owns the defaults and crosses process / worker boundaries. This PR replaces consumer-local defaults and optional threshold options with required sections; implementations stay in apps/cli.\nStated\nPR: omitted composition must not recreate local defaults.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "05\nResponse deadlines\nComposition purpose selects 100 ms for a status observer and 250 ms for ordinary lifecycle / execution-status exchanges. Execute admission stays 5 s; acceptance clears that timer.\nStated\nPR: status observation and ordinary execution-status requests have distinct deadlines.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "06\nRecovery scopes\nNumeric counters replace fixed recovery control flow: 1 execution reattachment per call; 1 fetch-resume allowance inside each execute attempt. A failed fetch feeds completion failure; a reattachment gets a fresh allowance.\nStated\nPR: each reattached execute attempt needs its own fetch-resume allowance.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "07\nOutput + framing\nCapture, spool, disk decoding, socket codec, and both worker-side checks share the output slice: 64 KiB chunks / 256 KiB inline / 256 MiB result / 512 MiB aggregate. Control caps stay 8 MiB JSON / 256 KiB execution control.\nStated\nPR + policy record: require the slice throughout the bounded output path.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "08\nMemory + supervision\nDelete DaemonResourcePolicy and the second memory-cap input. Use the snapshot’s RSS / worker-heap thresholds for supervision, launch, and reporting; retain 250 ms supervision / 25 ms heap samples / 2 replacements in 10 min, then drain.\nStated\nPolicy record: one derivation, resource shedding before replacement, and a bounded replacement circuit.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "09\nStartup + shutdown\nRequired slices preserve coordination, heartbeats, polls, stop escalation, idle lifetime, and drain acknowledgement timings. Startup child-failure retry becomes numeric (default 1). The unused healthy-startup timeout option disappears; healthy warm-up remains unbounded.\nStated\nPolicy record: preserve distinct cadences and deadlines; progressing warm-up has no project-size deadline.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "10\nDiagnostics\nLogger rotation, queue capacity, and disconnected-trace retention now use policy: 10 MiB / 4 backups / 1,024 queued events / 5 min / 1,024 traces (effective trace minimum 1). Trace expiry remains separate from result retention.\nStated\nPolicy record: bound diagnostic storage and memory while retaining reconnect evidence.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "11\nTest-only bridge\n7 new shared adapters (plus local logger / spool wrappers) translate legacy test inputs into policy-backed constructors. Unit tests, e2e helpers, cleanup, and the benchmark switch imports. Production gets no compatibility overloads.\nStated\nPR: tests need small thresholds without restoring runtime tuning seams.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "SUMMARY",
      "text": "12\nEnforcement boundary\nThe meta-test expands its retired-name / signature scan across CLI production sources. It catches listed defaults and bypasses. The existing registry grace argument and transport write-chunk option remain; codecs still take required projected numbers.\nStated\nCentral ownership is stated. Retaining those two optional numeric seams is unexplained in the supplied material.\n+",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
